{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the stout of heart</b> — this is one whose thought is that he will prevail and no man can harm him. And the opposite of this: <b>the fearful and faint of heart</b> — fearful of everything, and faint of heart to destroy." "<b>Naked</b> — that his garments will be heavy upon him when he flees."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ורך לב להשחית' is elliptical; rendered hyper-literally without expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:52.025164271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}